# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

The `portainer_deploy` action rolls an image revision out to services of a stack (Docker Swarm or standalone) and optionally writes it into a stack environment variable, as the `portainer_deploy` resource does.

> **Requirements:** Terraform >= 1.14 (actions). OpenTofu does not support actions; there, and with older Terraform, use the [`portainer_deploy` resource](../resources/deploy.md), which runs the same operation when it is created.

## Example Usage

### Run it from a lifecycle `action_trigger`

```hcl
action "portainer_deploy" "release" {
  config {
    endpoint_id   = 1
    stack_name    = "shop"
    stack_env_var = "REVISION"
    services_list = "web,api"
    revision      = var.revision
    force_update  = true
  }
}

resource "terraform_data" "revision" {
  input = var.revision

  lifecycle {
    action_trigger {
      events  = [after_create, after_update]
      actions = [action.portainer_deploy.release]
    }
  }
}
```

### Run it on demand

```shell
terraform apply -invoke action.portainer_deploy.release
```

## Lifecycle & Behavior

- The action runs only when it is invoked: from an `action_trigger` on the events listed there, or with `terraform apply -invoke`. A plan lists the invocations it would run; nothing is stored in state, so there is nothing to destroy and no `triggers` argument is needed to run it again.
- It sends the same requests as the `portainer_deploy` resource does when it is created, with the same defaults, and fails the apply with the same errors.
- The summary of what was updated is shown as a progress message.
- The deployment runs within a 15 minute timeout, the resource's default.

